Diagnosis: all five failures are semantic mismatches with Spider gold conventions (over-narrow projection `SELECT Name` vs gold `*`, over-literal string filters — trailing space in `'Korea '`, exact title equality, wrong value column `'Bachelors'` vs summary text — and set-difference direction), not syntax errors. The harness never executes the draft, so zero-row results caused by literal/value mismatches go unnoticed even though a second policy call is available. Fix: stronger prompt rules for Spider output conventions + one execution check with a single repair call when the draft errors or returns 0 rows (with sample values from the offending columns to ground the fix).

